abstract: >-
  An interactive Shiny application and structured dataset for exploring
  roll-call voting behavior in the European Parliament from 2004 to 2022,
  covering four legislative terms and roughly 3,700 members. It combines
  data preparation, feature engineering, exploration, dimensionality
  reduction (W-NOMINATE, MCA, UMAP) and clustering (k-means, PAM, HDBSCAN)
  in one interface, without requiring programming knowledge.
